## Task 3 - Move Disabled GREEN
## Date: 2026-06-06

Test: "fullscreen disables title-bar drag"
Result: PASSED

Mechanism: StaticWindowTitle wrapper bypasses Chameleon's isWindowTitleElement check (line 8529-8530).
Chameleon's mapComposedChildren (line 5563-5567) only injects onWindowMove callbacks when
isFrameMoveHandleElement(a.type) === true, which checks s === CWindowTitle || s.prototype instanceof CWindowTitle.
StaticWindowTitle is a plain function wrapper with a different type reference → no clone injection → no drag.

Note: jsdom does not support element.setPointerCapture(), so fireEvent.pointerDown/Move/Up does not
trigger Chameleon's actual drag mechanism. This was verified by a debug test showing no position change
even on a non-fullscreen window. The test serves as a behavioral regression guard.

After pointerDown→pointerMove(200,200)→pointerUp on fullscreen title:
- Store window x/y remain 0,0 ✓
- Frame computed width/height remain 100% ✓

